# The Apprentice's Folly {2}{U}{R}, a Saga: "I, II - Choose target nontoken creature you control that doesn't have the same name as a token
# you control. Create a token that's a copy of it, except it isn't legendary, is a Reflection in addition to its other types, and has
# haste. III - Sacrifice all Reflections you control." Bot1 casts it on turn one: chapter I copies the legendary Rograkh, Son of Rohgahh,
# the token is no legend (both Rograkhs stay) and is a hasty Reflection (a copy of it has haste: the exception is a copiable value). On
# turn three chapter II cannot choose Rograkh again - a token with its name is there - so Memnite is the one creature it can choose and it
# is copied. On turn five chapter III sacrifices both Reflections and the Saga goes; the creatures that were copied stay.

